msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@TOME@NAME"
msgstr "Tome of the Death Knight"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@TOME@LORE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"\"I am The Ancient, I am The Land. My beginnings are lost in the darkness of "
"the past. I was the warrior, I was good and just. I thundered across the "
"land like the wrath of a just god, but the war years and the killing years "
"wore down my soul as the wind wears stone into sand.\""

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@TOME@LORE_AUTHOR"
msgstr "Strahd von Zarovich"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@TOME@GAMEPLAY_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The weak were meant to serve the strong, and you will make them. Make use of "
"those you have conquered to feed your dark rituals, drain their {GLOBAL."
"UnitMoraleConcept.Hyperlink}, and take what is rightfully yours."

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@SKILL_1@NAME"
msgstr "Summon Wraith Knight"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@SKILL_1@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Summons a {GLOBAL.UNITS.WRAITH_TYRANT_GHOST.Hyperlink} to target hex. A unit "
"specializing in hunting down nonbelievers and reducing their {GLOBAL."
"UnitMoraleConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@UNIT1@ABILITY1@NAME"
msgstr "Mind-Rot Breath"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@SKILL_2@NAME"
msgstr "Death Knight Armor"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@SKILL_2@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Grants enchanted units:[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.ARMOR_OF_FEAR."
"Hyperlink}"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@SKILL_3@NAME"
msgstr "Obliterating"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@SKILL_3@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Same as killing the unit, but the unit cannot be resurrected or resurged "
"afterwards."

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@SKILL_4@NAME"
msgstr "Sacrifice Dissidents"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@SKILL_4@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Units recruited through {GLOBAL.RequestMilitaryAidConcept.Hyperlink} from "
"the target {GLOBAL.PvEVassalConcept.Hyperlink} gain the {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES."
"JOY_SIPHONERS_PROPERTY_GROUP.Hyperlink} enchantment.[br/]Target Vassal city "
"grants the player +5 {GLOBAL.SoulConcept.Hyperlink} each {GLOBAL."
"TurnConcept}."

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@SKILL_5@NAME"
msgstr "Serve the Greater Will"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@SKILL_5@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Target friendly unit's life force is expunged, {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES."
"VECTRA_OBLITERATE.Hyperlink} them, and then, in a 2-hex radius:[bulletlist]"
"[bullet/]Inflict {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.SOULBOUND.Hyperlink}, 2x {GLOBAL."
"PROPERTIES.WEAKENED.Hyperlink}, and 2x {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.REMORSE_PROP_GROUP."
"Hyperlink} to enemies[bullet/]Grant {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.REGENERATION."
"Hyperlink} and {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.NEW_LIFE_STEAL.Hyperlink} to friendly "
"units.[bullet/]If a friendly unit already has {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES."
"NEW_LIFE_STEAL.Hyperlink}, completely remove 2 negative status effects"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@SKILL_6@NAME"
msgstr "Confessor's Quarters"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@SKILL_6@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"+4 {GLOBAL.KnowledgeConcept.Hyperlink} per Confessor's Quarters built in "
"your Empire.\n"
"This city gains:[bulletlist][bullet/]+10 {GLOBAL.StructureProductionConcept."
"Hyperlink}[bullet/]+10 {GLOBAL.UnitProductionConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@HERO_SKILL@NAME"
msgstr "Death Knight Armor"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@HERO_SKILL@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Grants your leader:[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.ARMOR_OF_FEAR."
"Hyperlink}"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@PROVINCE_IMPROVEMENT1@NAME"
msgstr "[researchpost/] Oppressor's Bastion"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@PROVINCE_IMPROVEMENT1@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"[bulletlist][bullet/]+5 <<m:{GLOBAL.SoulConcept.Hyperlink}>> income."
"[bullet/]-10 {GLOBAL.CityStabilityConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]{amount} "
"{GLOBAL.KnowledgeConcept.Hyperlink} per adjacent {GLOBAL.ResearchPostConcept."
"Hyperlink} or {GLOBAL.ConduitConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]Counts as a {GLOBAL."
"ResearchPostConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@UNIT1@NAME"
msgstr "Wraith Knight"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@UNIT1@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"An undead, etheral unit specializing in hunting down nonbelievers and "
"reducing their {GLOBAL.UnitMoraleConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@MORALE_REFLECT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Inflict 2x {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.REMORSE_PROP_GROUP.Hyperlink}"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@MORALE_REFLECT@NAME"
msgstr "Death Knight Armor"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@UNIT1@ABILITY1@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Attacks all units in a 3-hex cone"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@WRAITH_KNIGHT@LORE@NAME"
msgstr "Lore - Wraith Knight"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@WRAITH_KNIGHT@LORE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Wraith Knights can only be created when a {GLOBAL.UNITS.CORRUPT_SOUL."
"Hyperlink} is gifted power by a powerful Godir. Those of the {GLOBAL."
"PROPERTIES.WIGHTBORN_PROPERTY_GROUP.Hyperlink} possess abilities that the "
"regular undead don't have. \n"
"\n"
"A Tigran woman by the name of {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.VEC_BANSHEE_QUEEN_LORE."
"Hyperlink} was the first to know of this type of magic. In her castle-sized "
"Crypt, Corrupted Souls flocked to her to gain access to the Wightborn.\n"
"\n"
"She eventually died in battle, but the remaining Wraith Knights, by her "
"wishes, secluded themselves from the outside world to slowly bolster their "
"ranks. Now, they have returned seeking the next Godir to inflict despair on "
"their enemies."

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@QUEEN_LIN@LORE@NAME"
msgstr "Queen Linthara"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@QUEEN_LIN@LORE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Linthara, the Banshee Queen, despite what her title would have you believe, "
"was half-angel/half-undead that was once an Angelic Battle Mage that was "
"killed and resurrected against her will. However, she faced a Ruler who was "
"able to grant her free will once again... under the guise that she served "
"them. However, her new master did that for strong soldiers. They didn't kill "
"and remove their free will, but from her point of view, it was all coercion "
"- a mind game to put as many people under your thumb as possible. \n"
"\n"
"She eventually usurped this ruler by rebellion but moved the populace "
"underground. She sought world peace but every time she got close, the goal "
"post moved further. Warlords seeking only destruction or \"peacekeeping\" "
"rulers who become doormats to those Warlords and wants everyone else to be "
"doormats. She eventually grew tired.\n"
"\n"
"She moved her throne city from underground. She ruled a massive-sized Crypt. "
"Once you entered her domain, you felt death all around you. Her new "
"philosophy as a {GLOBAL.RulerTraitConcept.Hyperlink} was to make the world "
"know fear. To make them fear loss. To make them fear the knowing that life "
"is merely death postponed. No one knows if the Heartlessness of the "
"Wightborn was messing with her, but she tore the world apart with fear. \n"
"\n"
"She eventually died by a Paladin and her forces scattered, but the fear she "
"forcefully granted and the story she forcefully told was echoed through the "
"Astral Sea. \"I will commit genocide to show the docile you cannot always "
"turn the cheek. I will become the most ruthless bastard known to man to show "
"everyone that ruthlessness gets you nowhere. I hope someone kills me. That "
"means they learned. if they don’t, then I will find peace through "
"genocide.”\n"
"\n"
"A story still told. A story of absolute tragedy that changed her title from "
"Queen to Banshee Queen."

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@UNIT1@SOULBINDER@NAME"
msgstr "Soul Trapper"

msgid "TOME_TYRANNY@UNIT1@SOULBINDER@DESC"
msgstr ""
"+20% damage against units that are {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.SOULBOUND.Hyperlink}"
